    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "For one study conducted in the Netherlands by Been et al, 54 data were presented using multiple cut-­offs to define the pre-­ and post-­pandemic periods, with several different comparisons, making it difficult to select one comparison that aligned well with the other studies; we, therefore, included this study in the systematic review but not in meta-­ analyses. Khalil et al 9 had overlapping data for stillbirth outcome with another study; however, preterm birth data were not overlapping, so only preterm birth data were used in this review.",
      "reason": "The manuscript excerpt indicates that not all compatible results were used in synthesis for some outcomes (e.g., excluding a study from meta-analyses and using only non-overlapping outcome data), but it does not state this comprehensively for all compatible results within each outcome domain."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_10a_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "For one study ... with several different comparisons, making it difficult to select one comparison that aligned well with the other studies; we, therefore, included this study in the systematic review but not in meta-­ analyses. Khalil et al 9 had overlapping data for stillbirth outcome with another study; however, preterm birth data were not overlapping, so only preterm birth data were used in this review. ... As they reported Ontario data separately and for an overlapping period with Shah et al 49 , we extracted the data for Canada excluding Ontario from Liu et al. to avoid double counting of data.",
      "reason": "When not all compatible results were used, the selection process was described (e.g., exclusion from meta-analyses due to multiple cut-offs, using only non-overlapping data, and extracting sub-regions to avoid double counting)."
    },
    {
